   "body": "### See an app you like. Rebuild it as your own native Mac app.\n\nAgent skills that take a native macOS app from idea to your Dock. \nSwift and SwiftUI. Local data. No Xcode GUI.\n\n[](#requirements)\n[](#requirements)\n[](#skills)\n[](#install)\n[](#install)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n**[Quick start](#quick-start) · [How it works](#how-it-works) · [Skills](#skills) · [Specs](#specs) · [Install](#install)**\n\n \n\n## Quick start\n\n```bash\nnpx skills@latest add daveebbelaar/bama\n```\n\nThen ask your agent:\n\n```text\nClone my to-do app as a native Mac app.\nScreenshot every screen, write the user stories, and build milestone 1.\n```\n\nNot sure where to start? Type `/bama`. It looks at your project and picks the next skill.\n\n## How it works\n\n \n \n \n\n**1. Clone**\n\nYour agent opens the app you like and screenshots every screen. It writes a screen index.\n\n \n \n\n**2. Plan**\n\nIt turns the screens into user stories with checkable acceptance criteria, in milestones.\n\n \n \n\n**3. Build**\n\nIt builds one story per commit. Before each commit it snapshots every page in light and dark mode and runs the tests.\n\n \n \n \n\n## Skills\n\n \n  Stage  Skill  What it does  \n   Start     bama    Router: finds where you are and calls the right skill  \n    app-brief    Turns an idea into a one-page brief  \n    new-mac-app    A working app from a template: Swift package, SwiftData, build script, snapshot mode, git  \n   Plan     research    Parallel researcher agents: market, users, features, design, macOS APIs  \n    clone    Screenshots every screen of any app with computer use or a browser, writes a screen index  \n    user-stories    A backlog with checkable acceptance criteria, in milestones  \n   Code     swift-swiftui    Swift 6 concurrency, state, SwiftData, AppKit bridges, compiler errors  \n    os-integrations    Global hotkeys, menu bar, floating panels, window control, screen capture, Shortcuts, URL schemes, CLI, permissions  \n    performance    Measure, then fix: main thread, GPU compositing, images, Instruments from the command line  \n    improve-architecture    Finds hot spots as the app grows and refactors one step per commit, with behavior proven unchanged  \n    agent-cli    Optional: a command line and MCP server, so Claude Code, Codex, and scripts can drive your app  \n   Design     ux-design    Names, flow, where each feature opens (inline, popover, sheet, window), words, and accessibility, before code  \n    mac-design    Liquid Glass, layout, toolbars, menus, keyboard, type, dark mode  \n    design-system    Native look with an accent color people pick in Settings, then one set of tokens and one rules page  \n    layout-grid    A 4 pt grid with checks that fail on misalignment: a code lint, a layout probe in snapshot mode, and a grid overlay  \n    design-kit    Your own parts, not Apple's: three token layers, type, an icon set, every part in every state, custom window chrome, and a parts gallery  \n    design-from-app    Rebuilds the look of an app you like from its screenshots: measures sizes, type, and colors, then compares pixel by pixel until it matches  \n    app-icon    A Liquid Glass icon written as an Icon Composer file, checked in every look  \n   Ship     build-and-verify    Build, install, snapshot every page in light and dark, look at them  \n    test-mac-app    Swift Testing, an in-app self-test, a debug bridge an agent can drive  \n    improve-loop    Works through the backlog one story per commit until a milestone is done  \n \n\n## Specs\n\nNot sure what to build? [specs/](specs/) has 1",
   "score": 6.361302477572996
  },
