   "body": "# MOT Test procedure UK🚘2025: Explained & Check [Prepare] Guide to pass emissions successful\n# CarMic\n# https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pr0AkWVH5cg\n\n[00:00] The MOT test, Ministry of Transport or simply MOT, is an annual test of vehicle safety and exhaust emissions required in the United Kingdom for most vehicles over 3 years old. In Northern Ireland, the equivalent requirement applies after 4 years. More than 23,500 local car repair garages through England, Scotland, and Wales are authorized to perform testing and issue certificates. MOT test checks that your vehicle meets road safety and environmental standards. It is an\n[00:32] offense to use a vehicle of MOT test age that doesn't have a current test certificate on a public road. You can check the status of your vehicle on this web page. All you have to do is just enter the registration number of your vehicle. How do test works? During the important parts of your vehicle will be checked to make sure they meet the legal standards. You can watch the test from a view wing area, but you are not allowed to interrupt the tester. It isn't the same as having your vehicle serviced and doesn't check its general mechanical\n[01:04] condition. The test does not cover the condition of the engine, clutch, or gearbox. What car parts are tested in the MOT? These are some of the important parts of your car that will be checked in the MOT. As you can see, for example, exhaust emissions, exhaust system, brakes, tires, wheels, bonnet, registration plates, lights, windcreen, wipers, seat belts, body, fuel system, and much more. Checking body, vehicle structure, and general items includes that uh they are free from excessive\n[01:39] corrosion or damage in specific areas, and there are no sharp edges likely to cause injury. Toe bars will be inspected for securess, condition, inappropriate repairs or modification. Theote tester will also check that the 13pin electrical socket is working correctly, the speedometer is in good working order, the engine mountings are secure, the fuel system will be inspected to check that there are no leaks, the pipes and hoses are secure and in a good\n[02:12] condition. The fuel cap fastens and seals securely. You should make sure that the key is available as the fuel cap will need to be opened. The vehicle will be inspected depending on the age and fuel type of the vehicle to check that it meets the rules for exhaust emission. Diesel vehicles. Theote tester will refuse to test your vehicle if they think that the smoke test any damage your engine. You should tell them at the start of the MOT if you think this may happen. To reduce the possibility of\n[02:46] damage and increase the chances of passing, you should keep your vehicle maintained at all times. Have the cam shaft drive belt replaced at the recommended intervals. Go for the MOT with a fully warmed up engine. It will produce less smoke and is safer to test and not temper with the governor settings. The exhaust system will be inspected to check that it's secure and complete. A catalyst isn't missing where one was fitted as standard. It's without serious leaks and not too noisy. The\n[03:21] vehicle will be inspected to check that the mandatory seat belts are in place. They are suitable for the vehicle. They are in a good condition. They work properly. They are attached securely. The malfunction indicator alarms or dashboard warning lights will be checked for the airbags seat belt which remove the slack from a seat belt in \n[transcript continues in field-notes/staging/Pr0AkWVH5cg.txt]",
